# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore -- CSO research project (paper, analysis, replication package)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Template from unicef-drp/cso-toolkit: templates/gitignore/research-project.gitignore
# Guidance: docs/gitignore_guidelines.md (why each block exists, how to test it).
#
# Copy to <repo>/.gitignore, then check nothing tracked is now ignored:
#   git ls-files -i -c --exclude-standard     # should print nothing
#   git check-ignore -v <path>                # which rule matched a path
#
# The rule in one line: data never enter git; the provenance sidecars that
# say exactly which bytes each result came from always do.
# Later rules override earlier ones, so keep the order of the blocks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---- 1. Data folders: ignore the contents, keep structure and provenance ---
#
# `data/**` ignores everything below data/, sub-folders included. Git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so `!data/**/`
# re-includes the directories (a trailing slash matches directories only);
# after that, only the files named below come back.

data/**
!data/**/
!data/**/README.md
!data/**/.gitkeep
!data/**/*.provenance.json
!data/**/input_manifest.*

inputs/**
!inputs/**/
!inputs/**/README.md
!inputs/**/.gitkeep
!inputs/**/*.provenance.json
!inputs/**/input_manifest.*

# dw_api_fetch() cache and dw_use() frozen URL downloads
_apis/**
!_apis/**/
!_apis/**/README.md
!_apis/**/.gitkeep
!_apis/**/*.provenance.json

_frozen/**
!_frozen/**/
!_frozen/**/README.md
!_frozen/**/.gitkeep
!_frozen/**/*.provenance.json

# Microdata kept outside the repo (S:, Z:, Teams, Gitea LFS) get their
# sidecars under data/provenance/<path>/, mirroring where the file lives;
# the block above already tracks them.


# ---- 2. Data and cache formats, wherever they appear -----------------------
*.sav
*.dta
*.rds
*.RData
*.rda
*.parquet
*.feather
*.sas7bdat
*.zip
*.7z
*.gz
*.tar
*.h5
*.duckdb
*.sqlite
*.db


# ---- 3. Secrets and personal configuration ---------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.netrc
user_config.yml
.Renviron
# A template with placeholder values only may be tracked, e.g.:
# !_config_template/user_config.yml
# Do NOT ignore .Rprofile: renv writes its activation line there.


# ---- 4. Results -------------------------------------------------------------
# Small text results (csv, tsv, tex, md, json) and figures used by the paper
# are tracked, each with its .provenance.json sidecar. Large binaries are not
# (section 2 already covers the data formats). Scratch output stays local:
results/tmp/
results/cache/
output/tmp/
output/cache/


# ---- 5. R ------------------------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/staging/
renv/python/


# ---- 6. Python -------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/


# ---- 7. Stata --------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.smcl
*.stswp
*.dta~


# ---- 8. Quarto and LaTeX build files ---------------------------------------
.quarto/
_freeze/
_book/
_site/
*_files/
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.lof
*.lot
*.nav
*.out
*.run.xml
*.snm
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.xdv


# ---- 9. OS and editors -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.bak
*.swp
*.tmp
